diff --git a/features/active-count.feature b/features/active-count.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a282fe7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/active-count.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Feature: Active task counter
+
+  The footer counter shows the number of incomplete tasks, wrapped so the
+  count is emphasized, and uses correct pluralization of "item".
+
+  Scenario Outline: Counter shows the remaining count with correct pluralization
+    Given the app is open
+    And the task list contains <total> tasks of which <active> are active
+    Then the counter reads "<count> <noun> left"
+
+    Examples:
+      | total | active | count | noun  |
+      | 0     | 0      | 0     | items |
+      | 1     | 1      | 1     | item  |
+      | 2     | 1      | 1     | item  |
+      | 2     | 2      | 2     | items |
diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..91f453f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Clearing completed tasks
+
+  The clear-completed control removes every completed task, stays hidden while
+  no completed task exists, and resets the mark-all control when used.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes every completed task
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    When the user clicks clear completed
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is not present
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is present
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed control is hidden with no completed tasks
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear completed control is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed control is shown with completed tasks
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    Then the clear completed control is shown
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed resets the mark-all control
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is marked completed
+    When the user clicks clear completed
+    Then the mark-all control is unchecked
diff --git a/features/edit-todo.feature b/features/edit-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c64a5d5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/edit-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Feature: Editing a task
+
+  Double-clicking a task enters edit mode with the title focused; the edit is
+  saved on Enter or blur, an empty edit destroys the task, and Escape discards
+  the change.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Double-click enters editing mode and focuses the title
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    And the edit field for "Buy milk" has focus
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter keeps the new title
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    And the user changes the edit field to "Buy soy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the task "Buy soy milk" is present
+    And the task "Buy milk" is not present
+    And the task "Buy soy milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur keeps the new title
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    And the user changes the edit field to "Buy oat milk" and blurs it
+    Then the task "Buy oat milk" is present
+
+  Scenario: An empty edit destroys the task
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    And the user changes the edit field to "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is not present
+
+  Scenario: Escape cancels the edit and keeps the original title
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    And the user changes the edit field to "Buy almond milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is present
+    And the task "Buy almond milk" is not present
+    And the task "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/filtering.feature b/features/filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..72bbf94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+Feature: Filtering the visible tasks
+
+  The hash routes all, active, and completed filter the visible list, keep the
+  matching filter link selected, update as items change, and survive reload.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete tasks
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    When the user opens the "active" filter
+    Then the task "Walk the dog" is visible
+    And the task "Buy milk" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed tasks
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    When the user opens the "completed" filter
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is visible
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows every task
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    When the user opens the "all" filter
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is visible
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Completing a task hides it under the active filter
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user opens the "active" filter
+    And the user checks the task "Buy milk"
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: The selected filter link carries the selected class
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user opens the "completed" filter
+    Then the "completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists across reload
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And the active filter is "completed"
+    When the app reloads
+    Then the "completed" filter link is selected
+    And the task "Buy milk" is visible
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is not visible
diff --git a/features/new-todo.feature b/features/new-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9924214
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/new-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Adding a new task
+
+  The new task input creates a task when the user submits non-empty text,
+  appends it to the list, clears the field, and ignores whitespace-only input.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Submitting text adds the task and clears the input
+    Given the task list is empty
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter in the new task field
+    Then the list shows 1 task
+    And the list item "Buy milk" is present
+    And the new task field is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input adds no task
+    Given the task list is empty
+    When the user types "   " and presses Enter in the new task field
+    Then the list shows 0 tasks
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..28c0ecc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Feature: Persisting tasks
+
+  Tasks survive a page reload through localStorage, stored under the
+  tasks-vanilla key as items with id, title, and completed fields. Editing
+  state is not persisted.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Tasks reload from localStorage after a reload
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the app reloads
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is present
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is present
+
+  Scenario: Tasks are stored under the tasks-vanilla key
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage holds a "tasks-vanilla" entry
+    And the "tasks-vanilla" entry is a JSON array
+    And each stored item has an "id", a "title", and a "completed" field
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted across reload
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the task "Buy milk"
+    And the app reloads
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/todo-display.feature b/features/todo-display.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..28039ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-display.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Feature: Task list display
+
+  The app reveals the main list, the counter, and the filters only when at
+  least one task exists; with an empty list those regions stay hidden and the
+  new task field receives focus on load.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Empty list hides the main and footer regions
+    Given the task list is empty
+    Then the main region is hidden
+    And the footer region is hidden
+
+  Scenario: New task field is focused when the app loads
+    Given the task list is empty
+    Then the new task field has focus
+
+  Scenario: Tasks render as list items
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    Then the list shows 2 tasks
+    And the list item "Buy milk" is present
diff --git a/features/toggle-completion.feature b/features/toggle-completion.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..748473d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-completion.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Marking tasks complete
+
+  A single task toggles its completed state when its checkbox is clicked, and
+  the mark-all control toggles every task to match itself and reflects the set.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is open
+
+  Scenario: Checking a task marks it completed
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user checks the task "Buy milk"
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles every task
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    When the user checks the mark-all control
+    Then the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark all control reflects every task being completed
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    And the task "Walk the dog" is marked completed
+    Then the mark-all control is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all control is unchecked when any task is incomplete
+    Given the task list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And the task "Buy milk" is marked completed
+    Then the mark-all control is unchecked
